#!/bin/sh
# The AppImage ships its own fontconfig rules (etc/fonts/conf.d) and fonts
# (share/fonts) for hosts that have no working fontconfig of their own.
#
# This hook deliberately does NOT point FONTCONFIG_PATH at the bundled rules.
# It used to, and that is what produced
#
#   Fontconfig warning: We will not regenerate the cache because some cache
#   files were generated by a newer version (0x2012003) of Fontconfig ...
#
# on hosts whose fontconfig was older than the one used to build the AppImage,
# after which "sans" no longer resolved. The host's `/etc/fonts` is the right
# answer where it exists; `apps/kimi-desktop/src/main/index.ts` picks it, and
# falls back to the bundled rules only when the host has none. A user who wants
# to force the bundled setup can still set FONTCONFIG_FILE/FONTCONFIG_PATH — the
# main process leaves an explicit environment alone.
:
